final_answer {"found":true,"answer":"The primary technical architecture and consensus mechanism identified in the documents are:

1. **Architecture**: A blockchain-driven Peer-to-Peer (P2P) network where each Large Language Model (LLM) acts as a full node participating directly in consensus processes. The system uses a hierarchical structure with Core Cluster Nodes (CCNs) and Edge Cluster Nodes (ECNs) managed by the Hierarchical Secure Clustering (HSC) algorithm to optimize scalability and latency.

2. **Consensus Mechanism**: Weighted Byzantine Fault Tolerance (WBFT) consensus. In this mechanism, only Core Cluster Nodes actively participate in the consensus process, while Edge Cluster Nodes receive results via broadcast messages from their designated CCN. The consensus results are packaged into blocks and linked to chains maintained by distributed LLMs.","evidence":[{"docId":"arxiv:2505.05103#17","quote":"This network architecture not only enables collaborative interactions among heterogeneous LLMs but also inherently enhances credibility and trustworthiness through blockchain integration."},{"docId":"arxiv:2505.05103#17","quote":"Only CCNs actively participate in the WBFT consensus mechanism, while ECNs receive consensus results through broadcast messages from their cluster's designated CCN."},{"docId":"arxiv:2505.05103#17","quote":"The HSC algorithm therefore incorporates two critical parameters in the LLM feature vectors: trust value and communication latency."}]}
